s stay behind the main character, as if the person filming does not want to be noticed. The main character is unaware of the camera and never looks directly toward it.\\n\\nThe framing should feel imperfect and spontaneous, like authentic phone footage captured by a real bystander. Use subtle natural handheld shaking, tiny framing corrections, slight breathing movement from the person holding the phone, and occasional minor obstruction from people or objects passing through the foreground.\\n\\nDo not use professional cinematic camera movement. No perfectly stabilized tracking shot. No dramatic crane movement. No artificial cinematic composition.\\n\\nStart from a natural medium-wide shot from several meters behind the character. The filmer slowly and cautiously moves a little closer, or gently uses a small phone zoom, trying to capture the important detail on the character’s back. The movement should feel hesitant, observational, and slightly imperfect, as if someone is discreetly recording something interesting without the subject noticing.\\n\\nThe main character behaves completely naturally and independently: [MAIN CHARACTER ACTION].\\n\\nThe character is wearing [CLOTHING / APPEARANCE], with [IMPORTANT DETAIL ON THE BACK] clearly visible.\\n\\nLocation: [LOCATION].\\n\\nPeople around the scene continue their normal activities and do not react to the camera. Background pedestrians may occasionally walk between the camera and the main character, partially blocking the view for a moment, making the footage feel more authentic.\\n\\nUse realistic daylight or natural available lighting, ordinary smartphone exposure, subtle autofocus adjustment, slight focus breathing, natural motion blur, realistic phone-camera depth of field, real skin texture, realistic clothing folds, authentic shadows, and natural environmental movement.\\n\\nThe video should feel like genuine candid footage uploaded directly from someone’s phone, not a movie scene, commercial, staged production, or AI-generated video.\\n\\nMaintain perfect consistency of the main character, clothing, body proportions, location, and the detail on the back throughout the entire clip.\\n\\nImportant camera behavior:\\ncamera stays behind the subject,\\nsecret observer perspective,\\nsubject does not know they are being filmed,\\nnatural handheld phone movement,\\nslightly imperfect framing,\\nslow cautious push-in,\\nsmall natural phone zoom if needed,\\nminor autofocus adjustment,\\noccasional foreground obstruction,\\nno cuts,\\nno scene changes,\\nno dramatic camera movement,\\nno cinematic stabilization,\\nno morphing,\\nno flickering,\\nno duplicated people,\\nno changing clothes,\\nno warped body,\\nno artificial CGI look.\\nMake it feel slightly awkward and unplanned, as if the filmer suddenly noticed something unusual on the person’s back, quickly took out their phone, and discreetly started recording from behind.\",null,null,null,\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/asb/ANqvLOYG4LYLJeO4HdBhJYdsE_udRiMoljdEGA9DgBdvxHLC_xbuD-7otNpk2eWlwvqhBv9oZhR_hTBY4H-MLzMuiW8tU5SwtNoWhVp-sc9cUBcEXJqDVAAmRrcC7W8ErgP8xzwppu16RNpuWjFukmowruFVYbd3sVALP3u-2Cpl\",[null,[[\"abra_r2v_10s\",3,[5],null,1,1],[[null,4,\"ab123739-eaaf-4b2f-aa71-231027ef37ee\"]]],[[null,null,[[[\"Create a highly realistic vertical 9:16 smartphone video that feels like it was secretly and casually recorded by another person standing behind the main character.\\n\\nThe camera must always stay behind the main character, as if the person filming does not want to be noticed. The main character is unaware of the camera and never looks directly toward it.\\n\\nThe framing should feel imperfect and spontaneous, like authentic phone footage captured by a real bystander. Use subtle natural handheld shaking, tiny framing corrections, slight breathing movement from the person holding the phone, and occasional minor obstruction from people or objects passing through the foreground.\\n\\nDo not use professional cinematic camer